  "body": "Hello. I noticed an extremely small issue: the terms [form control `maxlength` attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fe-maxlength) and [form control `minlength` attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fe-minlength) should not be marked with the `element-attr` definition type in the source code. That definition type is only used for the actual defining instances of the content attributes.\r\n\r\nRemoving the `element-attr` definition types would maintain consistency with the rest of the spec. For example, the term [srcset attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/images.html#srcset-attribute) does not have that definition type, but its various defining instances do (like the ones [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-link-imagesrcset), [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-source-srcset), and [here](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#attr-img-srcset)).\r\n\r\n(I accidentally pressed the \"submit\" key on my phone while I was typing this issue the first time. I'm sorry if I caused any inconvenience to anyone.)",
